{
  "doc": "Reference certificate vectors for consiliency_spec.verify_certificate (SEMANTICS.md sec 9). Each case names the files passed to the verifier (paths relative to this directory) and the outcome it must produce. pass-demo is a grounded certificate over a fixture E(C) that was not measured reproducible, so it binds but is advisory, never authoritative. `bound` reports the desired-graph binding on its own: the tampered copy still pins the same graph, so it is bound but not valid. The tampered-summary payload is the genuine payload with its one (pass) finding summary rewritten as a prohibition failure and re-hashed: with the finding set it is not the SEMANTICS sec 12 projection (payload_projection); without it, its summaries do not roll up to the certificate's dimension state (payload_binding).",
  "vector_set_version": "1",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "pass-demo-bound",
      "certificate": "pass-demo/certificate.json",
      "desired_graph": "pass-demo/desired-graph.json",
      "ec": "pass-demo/ec.json",
      "finding_set": "pass-demo/finding-set.json",
      "payload": "pass-demo/payload.json",
      "require_authoritative": false,
      "expect": {
        "valid": true,
        "bound": true,
        "authoritative": false,
        "advisory": true,
        "spec_authority": "grounded",
        "overall_result_state": "pass",
        "failed_checks": []
      }
    },
    {
